  "market_context": "During a strong intraday downtrend on AUDUSD, price executed a sharp impulse decline, then retraced upward briefly before resuming the bearish move — occurring within the London/NY session overlap window.",
  "key_observation": "Price pulled back to the 0.5–0.618 Fibonacci retracement zone (approximately 0.6750–0.6765) after a sharp drop, paused there, and then continued downward — confirming the zone as a high-probability bearish continuation area.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a sharp downward impulse move on the 5-minute chart that broke prior structure (BOS).",
    "Step 2: Drew a Fibonacci retracement from the swing high (0.68300) to the swing low (0.67100) to measure the pullback zone.",
    "Step 3: Noted price retraced precisely into the 0.5 (0.67700) and 0.618 (0.67550) levels — the 'Gold Zone' — where it stalled and formed rejection candles.",
    "Step 4: Observed price resumed the downtrend after the pause, confirming the retracement as a bearish continuation setup."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Fibonacci retracements on lower time frames (e.g., 5m) can yield reliable scalping entries when aligned with impulse moves and structural breaks; the 0.5–0.618 zone is the highest-probability pullback area for trend continuation.",
